= Identity — Simple =

'''Identity''' means being the very same thing.

Two identical-looking coins are not one coin. They may look the same, but there are still two of them.

That is the difference between:

* '''same thing''' — numerical identity;
* '''same qualities''' — similarity or qualitative identity.

Names are also not identity.

One thing can have several names.

Several records can accidentally use similar names for different things.

This matters in [[Knowledge graph/Simple|knowledge graphs]] because saying that two records represent the same [[Entity/Simple|entity]] can cause all of their information to be merged.

In OWL, <code>sameAs</code> means strict identity. It should not be used for things that are merely similar.

